# Draft review follow-up

- `useReviewRoomOwner.ts`: a room-acquisition HTTP 404 is a one-shot
  `observeAbsence()` dispatch. When pending writer evidence protects the review
  at that moment and is later withdrawn (the carry refused or filtered to
  empty), nothing re-observes the 404: the failed query keeps its old active
  data, so the review stays selected with no room and no room error. Retain the
  404 as an addressed absence the cache observation can reconsider when
  evidence clears, under the same generation horizon as a cached `gone`. Do not
  add a timeout or restart acquisition on every outbox change. Reproduced at
  `37b442f1f` (P2 in the docs repo's
  `work/draft-review-repair/review-fixes-d1-paint.md`); the 404 path is
  unchanged at `1dbbe8b52`; the scratch reproduction times out there, so it
  needs a fresh witness before the fix.
